  "stages": [
    {
      "stage": "1 admission",
      "description": "ObjWholeRead first calls ObjAdmitManifest(manifest,limits), preserving errors; successful admission is followed by ObjRawKeysValid(view,none). Admission checks limits, length, root/digest/id widths and frontier scales. No native certificate of this exact admission is established here."
    },
    {
      "stage": "2 range planning",
      "description": "ObjWholeAdmitted calls ObjRangeAdmitted(view,manifest,{start=0,stop=manifest.length},limits): actual range0..96, returned-byte budget and visit planning. It initializes output=[],visits=0,wireBytes=0,seen=[] then invokes ObjVisitRoots. Planning is separate from authenticated fetch."
    },
    {
      "stage": "3 parent authenticated fetch",
      "description": "ObjVisitNode fetches root scale1 through ObjAuthenticatedFetch/ObjRawLookup. ObjDecodeRecord checks the exact49byteparentwire through ObjDecodeRecordScale: scale<=37, exact wire length, valid bytes, then ObjNodeHash(scale,payload) and wireid comparison. HashWire computes actual node identity. AuthenticatedFetch also checks requested id/scale. A literal id cannot replace those checks."
    },
    {
      "stage": "4 three-child walk",
      "description": "Parent36bytepayload contains three12bytechildidentities in the pinned order. ObjChildIdentity/ObjVisitNode authenticate corresponding scale0 records, account visits/wirebytes/seen and consume32byteleafpayloads through ObjReadLeaf, retaining range/tail checks. Exact requested96bytes syntactically match childpayload concatenation; actual production traversal remains a proof obligation."
    },
    {
      "stage": "5 range finishing and manifest version",
      "description": "ObjRangeFinish checks outputlength, packages remainder/stats, and calls ObjManifestVersion. This encodes admittedmanifest then invokes ObjHashBytes. This manifest-version hash is a separate mandatory SHA computation from record-node hashes and final whole-data digest; it must not be dropped just because theorem projects bytes."
    },
    {
      "stage": "6 whole digest and original consumer",
      "description": "Only after range success, ObjWholeAdmitted invokes ObjHashBytes on actualread.bytes and compares digest.bytes to manifest.digest.bytes. Mismatch returns integrityFailure; hashfailure is retained. Success constructs ObjWholeVerified(bytes,version,stats). Original theorem matches fullResult and projects bytes only on success. The final original consumer remains mandatory."
    }
  ],
